While we're being blue sky, I'd go a lot further than this.

I'd like an interface option that was noun-verb instead of
verb-noun. That is <select noun(s) with pointing/selection
system><pick action by context of selected objects>
instead of <pick verb from universe of verbs><pick
noun(s)>.

More wordy because the set of nouns (your inventory) is
such that you have to have paging commands to choose
one--unless some can be hotkeyed, which they should be--
but more intuitive and probably easier to use, which
would be a Good Thing.

[And in practice, probably faster for people like me who
scan their inventory for what to do next, decide
it's something scrolly, possibly scan again with the
scrolls, remember the label of the scroll I want, enter
the verb, perhaps do a last paranoid check to make sure
I'll read the right one... then select the noun]

Probably still need pick up and drop as root-level verbs to
avoid insanity. Option for a 'use' command that does whatever
the obvious action is for the selected item: wands are
zapped, potions quaffed, scrolls read, tools applied,
weapons (un)wielded, rings (un)worn, etc.  Could be
a hybrid mode.

(I was sure I'd blabbed this before as a YANI but couldn't
find it).

